.TH SYS_PROC_CWD 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_cwd \- query process current working directory
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_cwd(pid_t " pid ", char *" buf ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_proc_cwd ()
attempts to copy the current working directory path of process
.IR pid 
into
.IR buf .
At most
.I len
bytes are written including the terminating NUL.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.
On error, a negative value is returned by the current implementation.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOSYS
Current kernel implementation is a stub.
.SH NOTES
Wired in native dispatch, currently unimplemented in kernel.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getcwd (2),
.BR sys_proc_exe (2),
.BR sys_proc_info (2)
